ilidad is a model designed to evaluate the fragility of patients through a set of criteria and accumulated deficits. It serves as a measure to assess the cumulative effects of various deficits, particularly in elderly populations. This index is crucial for understanding the overall health and vulnerability of older adults, allowing for better management and care strategies tailored to their needs.", "COHORTA PROSPECTIVA:A prospective cohort study is a research design that follows a group of individuals over time to assess outcomes related to health and aging.", "FENOTIPO DE FRAGILIDAD:El Fenotipo de Fragilidad es un modelo que clasifica la fragilidad en tres niveles: robusto, prefrágil y frágil, basado en signos y síntomas.", "PACIENTES FRÁGILES:Los pacientes frágiles son aquellos que presentan un alto riesgo de mortalidad y requieren intervenciones preventivas o terapéuticas.", "HERRAMIENTAS DE IDENTIFICACIÓN:Las herramientas de identificación son instrumentos diseñados para detectar la fragilidad en pacientes, como cuestionarios estandarizados.", "GROENINGEN FRAILTY INDEX:El Groningen Frailty Index es una herramienta utilizada para identificar pacientes frágiles, destacando su validez y sensibilidad al cambio.", "VULNERABLE ELDERS' SURVEY-12:The Vulnerable Elders' Survey-12 is a screening tool designed to identify vulnerable elderly individuals and assess their risk of fragility. This questionnaire aids in recognizing those seniors who may require additional health assessments, ensuring that their specific needs are addressed effectively.", "TILLBURG:Tillburg es una herramienta sencilla de identificación de pacientes frágiles, utilizada en la evaluación geriátrica.", "DEBATE ACERCA DE LA FRAGILIDAD:El debate acerca de la fragilidad se centra en la definición de fragilidad como un síndrome clínico y su evaluación en pacientes.", "VALORACIÓN CLÍNICA INTEGRAL:La valoración clínica integral es un proceso necesario para evaluar la fragilidad y determinar el perfil de riesgo de un paciente.", "CUESTIONARIOS ESTANDARIZADOS:Los cuestionarios estandarizados son métodos utilizados para identificar la fragilidad en pacientes, basados en diferentes modelos.", "REVISIÓN SISTEMÁTICA:\"REVISIÓN SISTEMÁTICA\" refers to a systematic review, which is a method of summarizing and evaluating evidence from multiple studies on a specific topic. This process involves an exhaustive analysis of the methods used to identify fragility in selected populations. Through this comprehensive approach, \"REVISIÓN SISTEMÁTICA\" aims to provide a thorough understanding of the available evidence and its implications for the topic at hand.", "PACIENTES ONCOLÓGICOS:PACIENTES ONCOLÓGICOS refers to individuals diagnosed with cancer who may require tailored dietary plans and specialized nutritional support during their treatment. This group of patients is particularly vulnerable to malnutrition, with prevalence rates that can reach up to 50%. The need for nutritional interventions is critical as these patients often face challenges that can impact their health and quality of life. Additionally, the evaluation of fragility in oncological patients can be beneficial for predicting treatment outcomes. Overall, PACIENTES ONCOLÓGICOS represent a specific population that necessitates careful nutritional assessment and support to enhance their overall well-being during the course of their illness."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}